  "issue": "ISSUES #128 \u2014 Intimidate / Trace record onto BATTLE_HISTORY->abilities[0] (the PLAYER's slot)",
  "oracleProfile": "battle-scene-off",
  "runner": "tools/run-mgba-probe.py",
  "probe": "tools/probe/probe-issue128-ability-history-off.py",
  "fixtureGenerator": "tools/probe/generate-issue128-ability-history-fixtures.ts",
  "seed": 305419897,
  "treeState": "stock ROM, port unchanged \u2014 this receipt was taken BEFORE the port fix",
  "freshRunCountPerArm": 2,
  "byteIdenticalAcrossFreshRuns": true,
  "source": {
    "recordTail": "src/battle_util.c:3194-3195 \u2014 AbilityBattleEffects ends with `if (effect && caseID < ABILITYEFFECT_CHECK_OTHER_SIDE && gLastUsedAbility != 0xFF) RecordAbilityBattle(battler, gLastUsedAbility);`",
    "caseIds": "include/battle_util.h:21/23/24 \u2014 ABILITYEFFECT_INTIMIDATE1 = 9, ABILITYEFFECT_TRACE = 11, ABILITYEFFECT_CHECK_OTHER_SIDE = 12, so both pass the guard",
    "battleStartDispatch": "src/battle_main.c:3880 `AbilityBattleEffects(ABILITYEFFECT_INTIMIDATE1, 0, 0, 0, 0)` / :3882 `AbilityBattleEffects(ABILITYEFFECT_TRACE, 0, 0, 0, 0)` \u2014 the literal 0 IS the recorded battler; neither case reassigns `battler`",
    "faintedActionsDispatch": "src/battle_util.c:1959-1960 \u2014 HandleFaintedMonActions state 6 passes the same literal 0",
    "record": "src/battle_ai_script_commands.c:643-646 \u2014 `void RecordAbilityBattle(u8 battler, u8 abilityId) { BATTLE_HISTORY->abilities[battler] = abilityId; }` (unguarded)",
    "consumer": "src/battle_ai_script_commands.c Cmd_get_ability \u2014 reads BATTLE_HISTORY->abilities[battler] FIRST and returns without drawing when non-zero; only the two-ability fallthrough draws `Random() & 1`"
  },
  "assertions": {
    "1_intimidateRecordsPlayerSlot": "INTIMIDATE arm: the AI's Mightyena (battler 1) holds ABILITY_INTIMIDATE (22), yet BATTLE_HISTORY->abilities == [22, 0, 0, 0] \u2014 the record lands on abilities[0], the PLAYER's slot, and abilities[1] (the real holder) stays 0.",
    "2_controlRecordsNothing": "CONTROL arm: an AI lead with a single non-Intimidate ability (Poochyena, ABILITY_RUN_AWAY 50) leaves BATTLE_HISTORY->abilities == [0, 0, 0, 0].",
    "3_traceRecordsCopiedAbilityOnPlayerSlot": "TRACE arm: Gardevoir (abilitySlot 1 = ABILITY_TRACE) copies the player Golduck's ABILITY_DAMP (6), and BATTLE_HISTORY->abilities == [6, 0, 0, 0] \u2014 the COPIED ability on the player's slot, again not the holder's.",
    "4_drawDelta": "Turn-2 HandleTurnActionSelectionState window, every Random() attributed to its caller by single-step: control = 14 draws of which 8 are Cmd_get_ability; intimidate = 6 draws of which 0 are Cmd_get_ability; trace = 6 draws of which 0 are Cmd_get_ability. The non-get_ability remainder is identical in all three arms (BattleAI_SetupAIData 4, BattleTurnPassed 1, ChooseMoveOrAction_Singles 1), so the 8-draw delta is exactly the `get_ability AI_TARGET` guesses that a non-zero abilities[0] short-circuits against the two-ability player lead (Golduck, ABILITY_DAMP / ABILITY_CLOUD_NINE).",
    "5_windowChoice": "The battle-lab checkpoint already sits inside turn 1's HandleTurnActionSelectionState run (the AI has committed BITE and Intimidate has already dropped the player's Attack stage to 5), so the first fully observable AI decision is turn 2's. abilities[0] is unchanged by then in every arm.",
    "6_controlFaint": "CONTROL arm caveat: the player's turn-1 HYDRO PUMP KOes Poochyena and the AI sends out MURKROW, so its turn-2 window belongs to a different AI battler. This does not touch the measurement \u2014 every counted get_ability call targets AI_TARGET (the unchanged player Golduck) \u2014 and the identical 6-draw non-get_ability remainder confirms the windows are comparable."
  },
  "portFindingAtReceiptTime": {
    "battleStart": "src/engine/factoryBattleStart.ts Intimidate loop (~:465-478) and Trace loop (~:484-513) write no aiObservedAbilityIds at all",
    "faintedActions": "src/engine/battleScriptFaintedActionsOrchestration.ts state 6 (~:418-465) writes the HOLDER's index (`index === id`), correct only when the holder is battler 0",
    "orderSites": "src/engine/factoryAiCheckBadMove.ts nextGetAbilityDraw (~:715) and checkAbilityAiTarget (~:772) test the trapper abilities BEFORE knownAbility; source order is history first"
  },
